{"id":"gap-G28","type":"text","x":48,"y":1528,"width":640,"height":632,"text":"**G28 / Recorder: memos folder never created and failed saves strand .part audio**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: With a mic strap and a card lacking /memos, the first recording fails; failed saves leave orphan .part files taking space.\n\nEvidence: board.c:592 mkdirs only watch and watch/logs; MEMO_DIR (con_memo.c:47) is never created. ext_audio_files.inc:85-100 opens \"<path>.part\" with no mkdir, so ENOENT gives HAL_REC_ERROR; con_memo.c:175-177 and 349 then show LIBRARY ERROR. record_finish (ext_audio_files.inc:120-136) keeps .part on failure and nothing unlinks it; the library lists only .wav. No free-space check. The recorder needs an external mic strap, so a bare B never reaches this.\n\nSuggested fix: Create the folder on mount, check free space before recording, recover or clean up .part files.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: app-recorder, drv-ext-hal, drv-sd\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-recorder, hw-strap, store-sd","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G28-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":1528,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Recorder**\nVoice memos: record 16 kHz WAV to SD (10 min…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). Recording survives leaving the screen.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Recorder|Open note]]","color":"3"},
