{"id":"gap-G29","type":"text","x":48,"y":2256,"width":640,"height":536,"text":"**G29 / Torch has no auto-off and ignores low battery**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A forgotten torch drains the battery to empty.\n\nEvidence: nos/apps/con_torch.c:217-218 (SCR_KEEPAWAKE), :88 (nos_keep_awake each tick), :57 (brightness override); nos_main.c:2080-2085 (keep blocks the timeout), :2226 (override beats user level and the low-battery path); power_policy.h:18-19. s_low_battery only toasts and disables AOD/wake. Nothing closes the torch. Exit by power button or back gesture not checked.\n\nSuggested fix: Add a Torch timeout and dim or close it at low battery.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: app-torch, eng-power-states\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-torch, eng-power","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G29-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":2256,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Torch**\nTurns the whole panel into a white or red…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). Keeps the display awake.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Torch|Open note]]","color":"4"},
