{"id":"gap-G25","type":"text","x":48,"y":14964,"width":640,"height":656,"text":"**G25 / Weather location cannot be set in NOS; Wi-Fi weather never starts on a fresh install**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A phone-less watch gets no weather and the hint points to a step the NOS build cannot do.\n\nEvidence: The only production caller of hal_weather_set_location is main.c:776, which is not in the build (CMakeLists builds nos_main.c). weather_service.c:93 skips every cycle while the location is invalid; :20 status \"Set weather location over USB\" is shown by out_weather.c:497-498. The BLE time-sync lat/lon (hal_esp32.c:884-891) feeds hal_location only, not the weather service. A paired phone can still supply weather (svc.c:1073).\n\nSuggested fix: Use phone-supplied lat/lon or add an on-watch city picker and fix the empty-state text.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: svc-weather, app-weather, drv-wifi, drv-hal-store\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-weather, app-weather, hw-wifi, store-nvs","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G25-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":14964,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Weather service (source merge)**\nTakes phone weather when it is under 3 h…\n\nruns: svc_tick wx_tick, checked every 10 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"3"},
