{"id":"gap-G25-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":15268,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G26","type":"text","x":48,"y":15716,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G26 / Unauthenticated /notify, /cmd, /media and /cover HTTP routes; server stays up on every STA connection**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Any LAN host can inject notifications, replace the cover image and inject media text.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:1739-1831 (handlers have no auth; /cmd is read-only, /notify caps app 19 / title 39 bytes, /cover needs exactly 125000 bytes); :1979 web_start on every GOT_IP; no httpd_stop. setup_authorized (watch_setup.inc:62) gates only /api/* setup routes. Reachable only on the same LAN while Wi-Fi is associated.\n\nSuggested fix: Token-gate or remove the routes and stop the server outside setup sessions.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: drv-wifi, svc-notifications, svc-ota\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): hw-wifi, svc-notif, eng-ota","color":"3"},
