{"id":"gap-G27-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":16420,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: Quectel EG800AK LTE**\nOptional LTE modem strap (AT commands, SMS).…\n\nruns: Hardware. Modem off 8 s after the last UI caller.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]"},
{"id":"gap-G27-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":16420,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Notifications service**\nStores up to 20 notifications, raises the…\n\nruns: svc_tick; banner pushed in the same tick.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|7 gaps]]\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G88","type":"text","x":48,"y":17148,"width":640,"height":656,"text":"**G88 / Phone link is unauthenticated: no bonding, static random address, NUS spoofable**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Nearby devices can inject notifications or calls, wipe alarms, and the watch is trackable by its fixed address.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:1558-1560 (sm_bonding=0, sm_sc=0, NO_INPUT_OUTPUT; deliberate per comment), :1485-1487 (same hardcoded static-random address on every unit), :1152-1155 (NUS RX has only WRITE flags), :1133-1145 (bytes fed straight to nus_rx_bytes). svc.c:1148-1191 dispatches notify, call, find, alarm, act, vibrate with no auth. Writing to RX is enough; subscribing to TX is not required. MAX_CONNECTIONS=2 (sdkconfig.defaults:47). Time-set path not confirmed.\n\nSuggested fix: Enable LE Secure Connections bonding, rotate the address and track the NUS handle.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: drv-ble, svc-phone-link, svc-alarms\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): hw-ble, svc-phone, svc-alarm","color":"3"},
