{"id":"gap-G88-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":17148,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Phone line pump and status reporter**\nphone_tick: drains NUS lines, tracks…\n\nruns: svc_tick on the UI task.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G88-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":17148,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Alarms service**\nEight alarms with repeat days, snooze (9…\n\nruns: alarm_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen-off.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|11 gaps]]\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G89","type":"text","x":48,"y":17900,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G89 / OTA accepts plain HTTP with no signature; /update exposes the session token**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A LAN attacker could push firmware during a setup session.\n\nEvidence: sdkconfig.defaults:65 (ESP_HTTPS_OTA_ALLOW_HTTP=y); sdkconfig:493-494 (secure boot and signed apps off); ota.c:340-343 (url_valid accepts http://); ota.c:455-485 (/update embeds the 32-hex token for any LAN client while a session is live); web_authorized (ota.c:144-155). Session lasts 600 s and starts only when the user opens Phone setup. Only SHA-256 and rollback protect images.\n\nSuggested fix: Require https, signed images, and do not render the token.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-ota, drv-wifi\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-ota, hw-wifi","color":"3"},
