{"id":"gap-G92-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":23364,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n52 B in-RAM preference struct loaded at boot…\n\nruns: RAM. Read by the engine every frame; written by apps then prefs_save().\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|15 gaps]]\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G96","type":"text","x":48,"y":24068,"width":640,"height":512,"text":"**G96 / Chat spend limit resets with each conversation (C only)**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Repeated new chats can overspend the tier target on C.\n\nEvidence: voice_chat.c:136-145 (clear zeroes cost_usd), :420-425 (allowance), :459,478,483 (messages say \"start a new chat\"); voice_policy.c:21-27 (allowance from that conversation's speech minutes); saved cost reloaded at voice_chat.c:184. No daily or device-wide counter. Deliberate per-conversation design; B has no audio.\n\nSuggested fix: Add a daily device-wide cap.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-chat\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G96-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":24068,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Chat**\nPush-to-talk voice assistant. On the 1.43-B…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). Carries SCR_KEEPAWAKE.\n\n`STUB` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Chat|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G21","type":"text","x":48,"y":24848,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G21 / UI task runs at lowest priority on core 0 under Wi-Fi/NimBLE/esp_timer**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Possible frame jitter during radio or worker bursts while the screen is on.\n\nEvidence: firmware/sdkconfig:1707 (main task pinned to core 0, default priority 1 inferred); NimBLE host at configMAX_PRIORITIES-4 on core 0 (hal_esp32.c:1531, sdkconfig:709); Wi-Fi (:1782), BT controller (:949), esp_timer (:1756-1758) on core 0; lwIP prio 18. nos_frame_priority.h mode 3 is off by default (nos_main.c:1307-1313, 1927). Flush (prio 4) and touch (prio 5) are on core 1. No measured dropped frames.\n\nSuggested fix: Enable the frame-priority mode or move services/radios to core 1.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: task-ui, eng-nos-frame, drv-ble\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): task-ui, eng-frame, hw-ble","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G21-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":24848,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**main / app_main UI loop**\nBoot, power-state machine, serial command…\n\nruns: core 0, prio 1, 8192 B. ON about 60 Hz (40 Hz authored); AOD/SENSOR 1 Hz frames; OFF 50 Hz loop, no frames.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G21-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":24848,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G21-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":24848,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**BLE host, advertising, GATT and bonding**\nNimBLE stack: advertising, connection…\n\nruns: NimBLE host task plus the 100 ms ble_control_tick callout.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|8 gaps]]\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G22","type":"text","x":48,"y":25552,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G22 / Any 1500 ms display queue/fence timeout reboots the watch**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A real panel or DMA stall reboots the watch mid-use, losing RAM-only state (tracks, timers, notifications).\n\nEvidence: firmware/main/nos_main.c:130 (DISPLAY_WAIT_MS 1500), :133-145 display_fault logs to RTC then esp_restart(); triggers at :146-150, :189-193, :233-244, :307/:336, :369, :436, :455/:468. Panel commands are retried 3 times first (:215-224). Comments at :135 and :240-241 say recycling DMA credits after an uncertain completion is deliberately avoided.\n\nSuggested fix: Retry or re-init the panel path first and restart only after repeated failures.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: task-flush, eng-nos-frame\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): task-display, eng-frame","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G22-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":25552,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**flush task**\nTakes 16-row stripe jobs, rotates them CCW…\n\nruns: core 1, prio 4, 3 KB, queue depth 3. Per dirty stripe; idle when nothing changes.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G22-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":25552,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G129","type":"text","x":48,"y":26232,"width":640,"height":536,"text":"**G129 / Nav stack edge cases: push during finger gesture does not reset owner; silent push/pull failures; air gesture overwrite**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Rare dismissal of a new screen, unopened screens, lost gestures.\n\nEvidence: nos/nos.c:303-325 (nos_push never touches P.owner; a back-swipe in progress keeps P.owner==1 against the new transition; plausible but not simulated), :305-309 (depth reject is logged to diag), :466 (nos_pull returns silently), :984-985 and :2334-2337 (single s_air slot overwritten).\n\nSuggested fix: Reset owner on programmatic nav and return codes.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-nos-frame\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-nos","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G129-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":26232,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G130","type":"text","x":48,"y":26864,"width":640,"height":560,"text":"**G130 / Clock/dt and timing inconsistencies: hal_millis freeze across tasks, off-screen dt, services 1 Hz alias, frame-stamped stopwatch**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Stale timestamps and up to one frame of stopwatch offset.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:65-66,111-146 (non-atomic frozen millis latched per frame, nos.c:2321/2464); nos_main.c:2091-2095 (OFF passes dt=1.0), :2113-2118 (AOD uses measured dt); svc.c:1303-1329 (1000 ms slow gate can stretch to ~2 s); svc.c:917-937 (stopwatch reads frame-latched time). svc_track.c:103 is unrelated.\n\nSuggested fix: Accumulate dt and use per-task clocks.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-nos-frame, svc-timer, task-ui\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-frame, svc-timer, task-ui","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G130-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":26864,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G130-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":26864,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Timer service**\nCountdown on a monotonic clock; rings the…\n\nruns: svc_tick each frame, 1 Hz screen off.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G130-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":26864,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**main / app_main UI loop**\nBoot, power-state machine, serial command…\n\nruns: core 0, prio 1, 8192 B. ON about 60 Hz (40 Hz authored); AOD/SENSOR 1 Hz frames; OFF 50 Hz loop, no frames.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G131","type":"text","x":48,"y":27520,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G131 / USB/host protocol robustness: stale .part blocks retry, path truncation, spaces, no framing timeout, aborted upload parsed as commands, help/allowlists inconsistent, stale host verbs**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Intermittent host errors and odd file names.\n\nEvidence: sd_xfer.c:537-543 (sscanf \"%127s\" cuts paths at spaces and truncates), :356-362 (existing .part gives \"SDPUT ERR staged\"), failure paths do not remove the .part; reserved_path blocks .part names (:285-290). Other ranges (nos_main.c:889-997, 1380-1805, watchctl.py, command_input.c:7) not opened.\n\nSuggested fix: Typed errors, validation and generated help.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: drv-usb-serial, drv-sd\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-usb-host, store-sd","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G131-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":27520,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**USB serial CDC, framing and guard**\nNative USB Serial/JTAG link. LF framing (191…\n\nruns: Read by the cmd task every 50 ms.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G131-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":27520,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**SD mount, lease and lock**\nMounts the card and hands out a mount lease…\n\nruns: board-fs retries a failed mount; leases taken per file operation.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|17 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G75","type":"text","x":48,"y":28200,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G75 / OTA/shutdown read-only scope freezes services, touch and UI during SD transfers**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Large BLE uploads make the watch unresponsive and can gap alarms or recording.\n\nEvidence: sd_xfer.c:121-131,547 (sdput/sdput!/sdrm hold OTA owner 2 for the transfer); ota.c:75-79; nos_main.c:1984 (mutate=0), :2072-2075, :2094, :2098, :2110, :2155 (touch, button, prefs_tick, nos_bg_tick skipped; frames run read-only). Deliberate (ota.c:72-74) and lasts only for one transfer. Alarm and track tick timing not traced.\n\nSuggested fix: Use a narrower SD lock and keep a minimal alarm/record tick under read-only.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-ota, drv-sd, svc-alarms, svc-workout\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-ota, store-sd, svc-alarm, svc-workout","color":"5"},
