{"id":"gap-G84","type":"text","x":48,"y":31524,"width":640,"height":560,"text":"**G84 / No magnetic declination; Compass heading is magnetic while Navigate subtracts it from a true bearing**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Bearings are off by the local declination, many degrees in some regions.\n\nEvidence: hal_ext.h:193 (\"0 = magnetic north\"); ext_mag.c:177-180 (atan2f, no offset); out_nav.c:659-668 (want = home_brg - head, GPS bearing is true); GPS-course fallback (head_src=2) is true-referenced. No declination code anywhere; docs/os-map/systems/Utility apps.md:62 wrongly claims declination.\n\nSuggested fix: Apply a GPS-derived declination and show true/magnetic.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-compass, app-navigate, hw-strap-mag, hw-strap-gps\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-compass, app-navigate, hw-mag, hw-gps","color":"3"},
