{"id":"gap-G133-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":32220,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**QMI8658 IMU (0x6B)**\n6-axis accelerometer/gyro, INT on GPIO8 (not…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read about 150 times/s by board-sense, with the screen on or off.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|4 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G133-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":32220,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**flush task**\nTakes 16-row stripe jobs, rotates them CCW…\n\nruns: core 1, prio 4, 3 KB, queue depth 3. Per dirty stripe; idle when nothing changes.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G134","type":"text","x":48,"y":32852,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G134 / Compass/Level polish: false calibration prompt on first open, partial calibration saved on leave, magnetometer runs in Level mode, axis map serial-only**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Weaker calibration and wasted power.\n\nEvidence: out_compass.c:196-215 (cold open reads calibrated=0 and shows the CAL prompt; leaving calls hal_mag_calibrate(0) and logs CANCELLED), :347 (mag polled in Level mode); ext_mag.c:246-262 (accepts calibration at >=10 of 20 bins and overwrites the old one; save unchecked), :285-298 (axis map serial-only).\n\nSuggested fix: Confirm saves and skip the magnetometer in Level.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-compass, hw-strap-mag\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-compass, hw-mag","color":"5"},
