{"id":"gap-G83-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":34564,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**PCF85063 RTC (0x51)**\nBattery-backed calendar chip on shared I2C.…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read once at boot; written when board_clock_changed is set.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G85","type":"text","x":48,"y":34988,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G85 / Compass heading silently degraded: blank dial while speaker plays, flat-tilt assumption, no interference warning**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Heading vanishes or errs with no explanation.\n\nEvidence: ext_mag.c:204 (sampling skipped while haptic or amp is on), :218-226 (valid clears after 500 ms), :157-162 (flat gravity fallback when the IMU read fails); out_compass.c:339,669-672 (\"Not connected\" is the wrong message), :534 (field strength only in a pill); set_diag.c:379-380 (field range check only in diagnostics). The amp is on only with an external audio module. Not bench-run.\n\nSuggested fix: Hold the last heading, flag stale tilt and warn on abnormal field.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-compass, hw-strap-mag, hw-strap-audio\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-compass, hw-mag, hw-speaker","color":"5"},
