{"id":"gap-G09","type":"text","x":48,"y":49964,"width":640,"height":704,"text":"**G09 / Screen never turns off with default settings: sensor_idle overrides the Always-on display setting**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: The AOD tile/setting appears to do nothing, the OLED stays lit and battery drains faster than expected.\n\nEvidence: nos/power_policy.h:13-14 returns SENSOR whenever sensor_idle is set, before looking at aod; prefs.c:159 defaults sensor_idle=1, :144 aod=0, :171 forces sensor_idle=1 on migration. nos_main.c:2085 uses it; PWR_SENSOR runs the dim 1 Hz AOD-style face (nos_main.c:705, 2106, 2225). The AOD toggles (set_settings.c:455,526; sys_control.c:231) change only aod. The only sensor_idle toggle is \"IDLE 80MHz\" in fit_energy.c:155,247. The panel is dimmed, not full brightness.\n\nSuggested fix: Make idle policy one visible setting (Off / Always-on / Sensor idle) and default to OFF when AOD is off.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: eng-power-states, store-nos-prefs, sys-control-center, app-energy, face-dot\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-power, store-prefs, sys-control-center, app-energy, face-dot","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G09-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":49964,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\nState machine in the UI loop. ON renders;…\n\nruns: UI task loop, every pass (20 ms delay when not ON).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
