{"id":"gap-G13","type":"text","x":48,"y":52340,"width":640,"height":680,"text":"**G13 / Battery percentage consumed without validity check (false 50% at boot, stale values)**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Header and phone can show a number while the Battery page shows \"--\"; briefly a false 50% after boot or unplug.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:287 (seed 50), :350-363 (battery_valid after 10 stable samples), :378-388 (hal_power_get keeps percent), svc.c:164 (sends bat to phone unchecked), sys_home.c:474, sys_control.c:345, sys_power.c:168, set_settings.c:603, set_modules.c:795,1186, set_about.c:99-101 all skip validity; only set_battery.c:38-42 honours it. The placeholder is short-lived and the low-battery policy (power_policy.h:9-10) does check validity.\n\nSuggested fix: Route every consumer through one helper returning unknown when !battery_valid; persist the last percent.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: hw-battery-adc, sys-power, sys-control-center, sys-home, sys-modules, sys-battery, sys-about, svc-phone-link, face-registry\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): hw-battery, sys-power, sys-control-center, sys-home, sys-modules, sys-battery, sys-about, svc-phone, face-registry","color":"3"},
