{"id":"gap-G14-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":53292,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Workout session engine**\nRuns sessions (start/pause/lap/finish),…\n\nruns: workout_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen off; checkpoint 30 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G14-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":53292,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**SD mount, lease and lock**\nMounts the card and hands out a mount lease…\n\nruns: board-fs retries a failed mount; leases taken per file operation.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|17 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G15","type":"text","x":48,"y":54020,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G15 / Alarms and timers cannot wake a powered-off watch (deep sleep wakes only on GPIO0)**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: An alarm set before POWER OFF silently never rings.\n\nEvidence: nos_main.c:809-811 (restart, otherwise only esp_sleep_enable_ext0_wakeup(GPIO0) then deep sleep); no timer, ext1 or GPIO15 wake anywhere in nos/ or firmware/main; pins.h:56 defines PIN_RTC_INT unused. svc.c:826-853 alarm_tick needs an awake CPU and an exact-minute match; no catch-up. sys_power.c has no alarm warning. Display sleep keeps alarms working; only POWER OFF is affected.\n\nSuggested fix: Arm RTC alarm/timer wake plus GPIO15 ext1 before deep sleep, or warn when alarms are armed and report missed alarms at boot.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: svc-alarms, hw-pcf85063-rtc, eng-power-states, sys-power\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-alarm, hw-rtc, eng-power, sys-power","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G15-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":54020,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Alarms service**\nEight alarms with repeat days, snooze (9…\n\nruns: alarm_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen-off.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|11 gaps]]\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"3"},
