{"id":"gap-G50-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":55052,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G122","type":"text","x":48,"y":55476,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G122 / Power polish: USB plug-in cue, SP_DEEP_SLEEP never emitted, cpu_mode retry spam, stale-age clause, 100 ms BLE callout, heap diag while off**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Missing plug-in cue and small standby costs.\n\nEvidence: sports.h:12 SP_DEEP_SLEEP has no emitter; power_policy.h:9-10 age clause unreachable because hal_esp32.c:385-386 clears sample_valid at 3 s; nos_main.c:634-646 cpu_mode retries every 1 s and emits a record on each failure; hal_esp32.c:1368-1371 BLE callout re-arms forever; deep sleep sets only ext0 with no gpio hold (nos_main.c:~810); no wake or cue on external_power 0 to 1. Heap-diag-while-off not checked.\n\nSuggested fix: Latch failures, stop re-arming, add the cue and measure deep sleep.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-power-states, hw-battery-adc, drv-ble\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-power, hw-battery, hw-ble","color":"5"},
