{"id":"gap-G48","type":"text","x":48,"y":57588,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G48 / Battery percent is an uncalibrated OCV estimate; calibration serial-only, wobbles, lost on reboot**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Percent can jump a few points on wake/sleep, may never appear, and cannot be corrected on the watch.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:299-308 (piecewise OCV table), :361 (+25/+10 mV load allowance toggled with power state, nos_main.c:701), no hysteresis; nos_main.c:1607 (batcal serial only); hal_esp32.c:2344-2345 and :356 (no s_cali means battery_valid never set). \"Lost on reboot\" is wrong: bat_cal is saved and reloaded (hal_esp32.c:314,318).\n\nSuggested fix: Monotone-discharge filter with hysteresis, persist the last percent, surface calibration errors.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: hw-battery-adc, sys-battery, sys-power\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): hw-battery, sys-battery, sys-power","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G48-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":57588,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Battery ADC (GPIO4, divider 3)**\nMeasures the system rail on GPIO4 (ADC1 ch3,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Sampled once a second by the battery sampler.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
