{"id":"gap-G79-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":61504,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Face registry and shared kit**\nCompile-time table of nine faces, AOD burn-…\n\nruns: UI task, only when Home page 0 or the face picker is on top.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|8 gaps]]\n[[Face registry and shared face kit|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G80","type":"text","x":48,"y":61904,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G80 / Raw heap_caps allocations bypass the PSRAM budget**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: The 6656 KiB budget undercounts, and some UI caches may fail instead of degrading.\n\nEvidence: Raw SPIRAM allocations: voice_chat.c:53, sports.c:303,305, workout.c:772, hal_esp32.c:1524 and :2262, native_menu_assets.c, main.c:1084, nos_main.c:1258; hal_big_alloc (hal_esp32.c:1594-1597) has no internal fallback; psram.c:49-54 checks the 1 MiB floor against free SPIRAM at each nos_mem_alloc call, so NOS callers are still protected. Whether callers degrade cleanly on NULL not verified.\n\nSuggested fix: Route allocations through nos_mem_alloc with fallbacks.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-render, drv-ext-hal\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-render, hw-strap","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G80-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":61904,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Scene record, damage diff and stripe raster**\nScreens draw into a recorded command list;…\n\nruns: UI task, each presented frame (AOD 1 Hz).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
