{"id":"gap-G18-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":62756,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Heart aggregation service**\nCombines the live locked reading, the…\n\nruns: heart_tick every 60 s on the UI task.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G19","type":"text","x":48,"y":63460,"width":640,"height":680,"text":"**G19 / Notifications do not wake the display; banner is deferred and stale at next wake**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A message arriving on a dark watch shows no sign beyond the buzz (nothing without the haptic strap).\n\nEvidence: power_policy.h:16-17 (wake only on touch, button, raise, knock); nos_main.c:2061,2091-2096; svc.c:230-233 notif_post calls nos_banner; nos.c:509-521 (banner sets active, plays feedback unless DND, calls nos_keep_awake, which only resets the idle timer, nos.c:585). Banner timer runs on nos_t (nos.c:2222), which is frozen in PWR_OFF, so the banner appears at next wake. The notification itself stays in the list and a haptic/sfx cue plays unless DND or no strap.\n\nSuggested fix: Optional wake-on-notification with a short ON window, or expire stale banners.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: sys-notifications, svc-notifications, eng-power-states, eng-nos-frame\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): sys-notifications, svc-notif, eng-power, eng-nos","color":"3"},
