{"id":"gap-G19-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":63764,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G72","type":"text","x":48,"y":64236,"width":640,"height":656,"text":"**G72 / Haptics and Sound preferences (and boot chime) do not apply to alarm, timer, call, find or volume detent**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Haptics/Sound off still buzzes for alarms and calls and plays the boot chime.\n\nEvidence: svc.c:699 (hal_haptic with no haptics check), :701 (only call sfx checks sound), :1188 (vibrate command). sys_boot.c:101 (boot chime unconditional), set_settings.c:2094 (volume detent sfx). Only nos_feedback (nos.c:571-572) checks the prefs; hal_haptic/hal_sfx gate on hardware and volume only. Muting alarms may be a deliberate safety choice.\n\nSuggested fix: Apply the prefs in ringer_tick and boot, and define the intended exceptions for alarms.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-alarms, sys-call, app-find-phone, sys-boot, app-settings, sys-modules\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-alarm, sys-call, app-find-phone, sys-boot, app-settings, sys-modules","color":"3"},
