{"id":"gap-G67","type":"text","x":48,"y":71796,"width":640,"height":656,"text":"**G67 / Call screen state gaps: outgoing/active calls untracked, declines read as MISSED, no call log, ring has no timeout**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Phone-side declines read as MISSED CALL, no End or timer for some calls, and an endless ring if the end message never arrives.\n\nEvidence: svc.c:1044-1068 (state 2 never opens the screen unless a ringing call was accepted), :977 (ring_screen), RING_MAX_MS (:47) applied to alarms, timers and find only; :1066-1067 (remote end, reject or missed all map to state 0); con_call.c:91 (missed = previous state was incoming); svc.c:1051-1057 (second incoming overwrites an active call), :943-950 (accept is fire-and-forget). A decline made on the watch is not mislabelled (con_call.c:467-469). No call log found in the opened files.\n\nSuggested fix: Model call states explicitly, add a ring timeout, call log and acknowledgments.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: sys-call, svc-phone-link\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): sys-call, svc-phone","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G67-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":71796,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Incoming call screen**\nPushed by the service on an incoming GB…\n\nruns: Pushed by svc_tick; keeps the display awake.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Incoming call screen|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G67-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":71796,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Phone line pump and status reporter**\nphone_tick: drains NUS lines, tracks…\n\nruns: svc_tick on the UI task.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G68","type":"text","x":48,"y":72548,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G68 / Phone link receive-side loss is silent; ring not flushed on disconnect**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Lost messages leave stale state; a phantom call or find ring is possible after link loss.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:1092 (s_nus_dropped incremented at 1114, 1124, 1212, never read), :1130 (overlong lines dropped), ~1421 (disconnect resets assembly only, not the ring); svc.c:1236 (LINES_PER_FRAME=8), :1222-1226 (disconnect clears find/call, but queued lines are handled afterwards). Bad JSON and unknown types are dropped without a log (svc.c:1200-1210).\n\nSuggested fix: Flush the ring on disconnect, count and log drops, raise lines per tick when idle.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-phone-link, drv-ble\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-phone, hw-ble","color":"5"},
