{"id":"gap-G73","type":"text","x":48,"y":75124,"width":640,"height":632,"text":"**G73 / No unsynced-clock indicator: faces, alarms and apps run from epoch 0 (1970)**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: A plausible wrong time with no warning, and alarms may fire on a bogus clock.\n\nEvidence: board.c:877-882 (clock set to epoch 0 without RTC, retained or phone time); hal_esp32.c:140-153 (hal_get_datetime has no validity flag); svc.c:826-851 (alarm_tick has no epoch guard). hal_epoch_seconds() returns 0 when unset and some screens use it (set_modules.c:777, set_settings.c:1916, set_diag.c:214, fit_workout.c:830), but faces and alarms do not.\n\nSuggested fix: Expose a clock-valid flag, show a not-synced glyph and gate alarms on valid time.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-time, face-registry, svc-alarms, app-world-clock, hw-pcf85063-rtc\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-time, face-registry, svc-alarm, app-world-clock, hw-rtc","color":"5"},
