{"id":"gap-G113","type":"text","x":48,"y":76752,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G113 / Saved volume and haptic strength are not applied to drivers at boot**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: After every reboot feedback ignores the saved level while Settings shows it.\n\nEvidence: ext_audio.c:337 (driver volume 70), ext_haptic.c:43 (strength 80); prefs defaults 60/70 (prefs.c:139-141). Only callers of hal_audio_volume/hal_haptic_set_strength: set_settings.c:1768-1769 (Reset), 2093-2096 (sliders), set_diag.c:634-643 (Diagnostics), ext_debug_commands.inc:44. None runs after prefs_load.\n\nSuggested fix: Apply both prefs after prefs_load in the boot sequence.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-settings, hw-strap-audio, hw-strap-haptic, store-nos-prefs\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-settings, hw-speaker, hw-haptic, store-prefs","color":"3"},
