{"id":"gap-G152","type":"text","x":48,"y":81376,"width":640,"height":560,"text":"**G152 / Documentation drift (PMIC_AUDIT, PHONE.md, SPORT_MODE.md, os-map notes, ui.h comments) contradicts code**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Maintainers cannot trust the docs.\n\nEvidence: docs/PMIC_AUDIT.md:36-38 cites nos_main.c:1322-1362 and :1340/1359, which are now a command parser and hal_setup_info; docs/SPORT_MODE.md:23 says there are no calorie claims while sports.c:171,391, background.c:155 and svc.c:46,445 publish kcal. PHONE.md frame-rate/storage contradictions not found.\n\nSuggested fix: Refresh in one pass.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-nos-frame\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-nos","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G152-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":81376,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G101","type":"text","x":48,"y":82204,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G101 / Knock-lock (default on) blocks call Accept/Decline and power-sheet buttons; knock-wake also locks**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: Users must knock twice before answering a call, and a knock wake can lock the watch.\n\nEvidence: nos/nos.c:666 drops new presses while locked (hint toast only, :630-635); nos/prefs.c:158 knock_lock=1; con_call.c:463 Accept/Decline are touch hits and gated; knock_tick (nos.c:646-653) toggles the lock on the first frame after a knock wake (nos_main.c:2047-2049). The physical button still silences a ring. Toggle-on-wake is partly intentional.\n\nSuggested fix: Exempt ring/power screens and lock only if already ON.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: eng-nos-frame, sys-call, sys-power\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-nos, sys-call, sys-power","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G101-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":82204,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**nos_frame_run / frame_run**\nPer-frame pipeline: input, nos_bg_tick,…\n\nruns: Called by the UI task each ON frame; 1 Hz in AOD/SENSOR; not called in OFF.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
