{"id":"gap-G01","type":"text","x":48,"y":88968,"width":640,"height":680,"text":"**G01 / Badminton/workout calories are zero or hidden by default (user complaint)**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: A recorded badminton game shows no calories unless the user first finds Sports setup and enters mass.\n\nEvidence: nos/prefs.c:134-175 (sports_mass_kg defaults to 0); nos/workout.c:274-279 (energy_kcal_est = MET*3.5*mass/200*minutes only when mass is set; badminton MET 5.5 at :65; elapsed time includes idle); nos/apps/fit_workout.c:631-635 (setup row says \"Not set / calories unavailable\"), :1013-1019 (energy rows drawn only when energy_kcal_est > 0). Only kcal display is the DETAILS block. No mass prompt at Start. HR and movement are not used. Zero default is deliberate and labelled.\n\nSuggested fix: Prompt for mass at first Start, always show an ENERGY row on live/summary/history, use Keytel when HR is valid and movement-scaled MET otherwise.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: app-sports, svc-workout, store-nos-prefs\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-sports, svc-workout, store-prefs","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G01-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":88968,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Sports**\nWorkout screen: pick a profile, start,…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). The recorder itself runs from svc_tick.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Sports|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G01-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":88968,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Workout session engine**\nRuns sessions (start/pause/lap/finish),…\n\nruns: workout_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen off; checkpoint 30 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G01-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":88968,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n52 B in-RAM preference struct loaded at boot…\n\nruns: RAM. Read by the engine every frame; written by apps then prefs_save().\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|15 gaps]]\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G06","type":"text","x":48,"y":89744,"width":640,"height":656,"text":"**G06 / No per-session movement/activity graph for workouts (user complaint)**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: No post-game intensity, movement or HR curve on the watch; offline needs a manual join.\n\nEvidence: nos/workout.h:70-96 (snapshot has scalars plus up to WORKOUT_LAPS_MAX laps, no series); history is 12 snapshots (workout.h:10); nos/workout_motion.c:9-52 only increments counters; no chart/sparkline code in fit_workout.c. The journal logs timestamped SP_HEART/SP_IMU/SP_GPS and tools/sports_export.py has --day/--start/--end, so a curve can be rebuilt offline by time window (manual join). Jobs window and exporter claims were not fully checked.\n\nSuggested fix: Store per-minute bins (movement fraction, mean bpm, kcal) per session, draw them in details/summary, export them.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: svc-workout, app-sports, store-sd-sports\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-workout, app-sports, store-sports-journal","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G06-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":89744,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Workout session engine**\nRuns sessions (start/pause/lap/finish),…\n\nruns: workout_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen off; checkpoint 30 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G06-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":89744,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Sports**\nWorkout screen: pick a profile, start,…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). The recorder itself runs from svc_tick.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Sports|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G06-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":89744,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**SD sports journal (.spt)**\n/sdcard/watch/sports/YYYYMMDD-events.spt and…\n\nruns: SD. Drained every 1 s by sports_sd.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G07","type":"text","x":48,"y":90496,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G07 / Workout calories never reach the daily Activity/Energy totals**\n\n`MEDIUM`\n\nImpact: An hour of badminton adds ~400 kcal to nothing; the day total misses it.\n\nEvidence: nos/workout.c:276-278 computes energy_kcal_est; consumers are only fit_workout.c:1013-1014 (DETAILS), background.c:154-155 (Jobs trace) and the sim. nos/svc.c:445 sets daily kcal = steps*KCAL_STEP with no workout term; fit_energy.c:144, fit_activity.c:406 and face_segment.c:263 read that value. Pedometer rejection of racket motion not verified. Gross MET energy includes resting metabolism, so a straight merge needs a design decision.\n\nSuggested fix: Merge session net energy into the daily total and subtract session steps to avoid double counting.\n\nVotes: 2/2\n\nNodes: svc-workout, svc-activity, app-energy\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G07-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":90496,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Workout session engine**\nRuns sessions (start/pause/lap/finish),…\n\nruns: workout_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen off; checkpoint 30 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
