{"id":"gap-G52","type":"text","x":48,"y":98972,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G52 / Activity buckets (nosact) not flushed at shutdown/OTA; checkpoint status unread**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Up to 10 minutes of hourly and active-minute data lost or mis-binned.\n\nEvidence: svc.c:496-509,527,558 (act_save every 10 min or at rollover); nos_main.c:763-800 and board.c:931-936 flush prefs, voice, sports and pedometer but not nosact; svc.h:99-100 checkpoint fields have no reader. A failed save emits a diag event (svc.c:502). Pedometer total is saved separately.\n\nSuggested fix: Add a flush to the shutdown/OTA barrier and expose checkpoint errors in diagnostics.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-activity, drv-hal-store, eng-power-states\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-activity, store-nvs, eng-power","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G52-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":98972,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Activity service (svc_activity)**\nTurns pedometer output into daily steps, km,…\n\nruns: act_tick 1 Hz on the UI task, also screen off. Checkpoint every 10 min when dirty.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G52-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":98972,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G52-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":98972,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\nState machine in the UI loop. ON renders;…\n\nruns: UI task loop, every pass (20 ms delay when not ON).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G53","type":"text","x":48,"y":99652,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G53 / Synchronous NVS/SD writes (nosact, alarms, tuning, sports, prefs) run on the UI task**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Possible frame hitch of tens to hundreds of ms when a save lands.\n\nEvidence: svc.c:496-508,721-728, sports.c:347, tuning.c:40 save inline via hal_store_save_checked; hal_esp32.c:177-257 (nvs_commit in the caller's task). Prefs defer via a dirty flag (prefs.c:260-265, 365-382) but also flush on the UI task and with heavier SD work, so \"unlike prefs\" is wrong. Stall length unmeasured; saves are infrequent.\n\nSuggested fix: Gate through the board-fs persistence window or a worker with an internal stack.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: task-ui, drv-hal-store, svc-activity, store-nos-prefs\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): task-ui, store-nvs, svc-activity, store-prefs","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G53-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":99652,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**main / app_main UI loop**\nBoot, power-state machine, serial command…\n\nruns: core 0, prio 1, 8192 B. ON about 60 Hz (40 Hz authored); AOD/SENSOR 1 Hz frames; OFF 50 Hz loop, no frames.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G53-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":99652,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G53-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":99652,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Activity service (svc_activity)**\nTurns pedometer output into daily steps, km,…\n\nruns: act_tick 1 Hz on the UI task, also screen off. Checkpoint every 10 min when dirty.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G53-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":99980,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n52 B in-RAM preference struct loaded at boot…\n\nruns: RAM. Read by the engine every frame; written by apps then prefs_save().\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|15 gaps]]\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G54","type":"text","x":48,"y":100356,"width":640,"height":680,"text":"**G54 / Several saves are unchecked or never retried: alarms, world clock, sea-level ref, compass cal, battery cal, Control Center prefs**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: An alarm, calibration or reference could silently revert after reboot if the NVS write fails (rare).\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:256-257 (void hal_store_save drops the result); time_worldclock.c:60, ext_mag.c:260, hal_esp32.c:314 use it; svc.c:721-731 (checked, but failure only traced); out_baro.c:686-692 (SAVED shown unconditionally). Control Center uses prefs_save, which retries every 5 s (prefs.c:260-264, 345-381), so only the user-facing error is missing. These keys are NVS-only.\n\nSuggested fix: Use hal_store_save_checked with dirty/retry state and surface failure.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: svc-alarms, app-world-clock, app-barometer, hw-strap-mag, sys-control-center, drv-hal-store\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): svc-alarm, app-world-clock, app-barometer, hw-mag, sys-control-center, store-nvs","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":100356,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Alarms service**\nEight alarms with repeat days, snooze (9…\n\nruns: alarm_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen-off.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|11 gaps]]\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":100356,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**World clock**\nUp to four favourite cities from a table of…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[World clock|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":100356,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Barometer**\nPressure with 3 h trend and 24 h chart,…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Barometer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":100660,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: QMC5883L/HMC5883L compass**\nOptional magnetometer strap for the Compass…\n\nruns: Hardware. Sampled only while a consumer asks.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-4","type":"text","x":1224,"y":100660,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Control Center**\nSystem sheet dropped from the face: eleven…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition).\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Control Center|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G54-component-5","type":"text","x":1680,"y":100660,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G55","type":"text","x":48,"y":101132,"width":640,"height":536,"text":"**G55 / sportstune and wake_cfg are NVS-only, violating the SD-authoritative settings rule**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Tuning is lost on an NVS erase and survives Reset inconsistently.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:238 (only nosprefs and wifi_cred route to SD), :253; nos/tuning.c:18,40 and core/wake_service.c:57,63 use hal_store; no reset code touches either key. Saves are checked. Whether the SD-authoritative rule covers every key is not confirmed.\n\nSuggested fix: Fold into the SD checkpoint or add SD routing.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: store-nos-prefs, drv-hal-store, app-settings\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): store-prefs, store-nvs, app-settings","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G55-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":101132,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n52 B in-RAM preference struct loaded at boot…\n\nruns: RAM. Read by the engine every frame; written by apps then prefs_save().\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|15 gaps]]\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G55-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":101132,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G55-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":101132,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Settings**\n30-row preference list in six sections.…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). Prewarmed from Home on odd frames.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Settings|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G56","type":"text","x":48,"y":101764,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G56 / NVS health invisible: init failure ignored, capacity gauge boot-time with wrong denominator**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: NVS-only data can revert to defaults for a boot with no notice; the gauge shows an optimistic stale value.\n\nEvidence: hal_esp32.c:2316-2322 (NO_FREE_PAGES/NEW_VERSION_FOUND only logged, deliberately not erased); board.c:517-533,923 (stats read once at boot); set_modules.c:1307,1314 (percent from that snapshot). partitions.csv:5 gives 756 entries but about 630 are usable, so the percent is optimistic. B's primary settings are on SD.\n\nSuggested fix: Expose an NVS-unavailable flag, refresh the gauge against available entries, keep no-silent-erase.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: drv-hal-store, sys-modules\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): store-nvs, sys-modules","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G56-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":101764,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G56-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":101764,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Modules**\nStatus board for 16 parts (7 board, 9 strap)…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). 1 Hz refresh.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|8 gaps]]\n[[Modules|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G57","type":"text","x":48,"y":102468,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G57 / NVS or RTC save failure can block shutdown/restart**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: With NVS full or an RTC fault the watch cannot power off or restart cleanly via the UI.\n\nEvidence: board.c:903-912 (failed pedometer save returns 0), :935-946, :1150-1152 (sleep_failed on !fs_ok or dirty RTC), :801-828 (rtc_maintain); firmware/main/nos_main.c:798-801 (cancels shutdown, DIAG_SLEEP_BLOCK 16). Other esp_restart paths (nos_main.c:144, 836, ota.c) bypass it. rtc_maintain retries every 5 s. Fails safe by design.\n\nSuggested fix: Retry once, time-limit the flush and proceed after logging.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: task-board-fs, drv-hal-store, hw-pcf85063-rtc, eng-power-states\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): task-board-fs, store-nvs, hw-rtc, eng-power","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G57-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":102468,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**board-fs task**\nDevice retry, SD mount retry, pedometer NVS…\n\nruns: prio 1, 4 KB. 100 ms loop, always on.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|1 gap]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G57-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":102468,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**hal_store (NVS + SD routing)**\nBlob API over NVS namespace 'wos'. Only…\n\nruns: Called inline by the owner of each key (UI task or board-fs).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|10 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G57-component-2","type":"text","x":1680,"y":102468,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**PCF85063 RTC (0x51)**\nBattery-backed calendar chip on shared I2C.…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read once at boot; written when board_clock_changed is set.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G57-component-3","type":"text","x":768,"y":102772,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\nState machine in the UI loop. ON renders;…\n\nruns: UI task loop, every pass (20 ms delay when not ON).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G58","type":"text","x":48,"y":103148,"width":640,"height":608,"text":"**G58 / SD transfer verbs: malformed args silent with ok=1; sdrm can delete txn/backup files**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Hosts believe failed verbs succeeded; leftover .part or .sdxfer-old files can be deleted.\n\nEvidence: sd_xfer.c:536-546 (failed sscanf returns 0 with no reply), nos_main.c:860-865 (DONE ok=1 unless an \" ERR \" line is printed), host_request.c:19-25; reserved_path (sd_xfer.c:283-289) applied on put but not on sdrm (~600-604). recover_transaction runs before sdrm (~563), so the backup-loss scenario is largely mitigated.\n\nSuggested fix: Return a typed ERR with ok=0 and refuse sdrm of journal files while a transaction is pending.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: drv-usb-serial, drv-sd\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): eng-usb-host, store-sd","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G58-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":103148,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**USB serial CDC, framing and guard**\nNative USB Serial/JTAG link. LF framing (191…\n\nruns: Read by the cmd task every 50 ms.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"gap-G58-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":103148,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**SD mount, lease and lock**\nMounts the card and hands out a mount lease…\n\nruns: board-fs retries a failed mount; leases taken per file operation.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|17 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"gap-G60","type":"text","x":48,"y":103852,"width":640,"height":584,"text":"**G60 / Energy/Battery history re-reads the full day journal every 10 s; drag-zoom can yield an empty range error**\n\n`LOW`\n\nImpact: Sustained SD/CPU load while open and a false error after extreme zoom.\n\nEvidence: fit_energy.c:70 (refresh every 10 s), :32-41; sports.c:465-520 (whole day file re-read, no cache); fit_energy.c:224-226 (integer-division zoom reaches start==end), sports.c:434 (rejects start>=end), fit_energy.c:38 (HISTORY UNAVAILABLE); :71-75 (Sensor logs poll each second). Only while those screens are open; the 180-200 KB size was not verified.\n\nSuggested fix: Cache bins, enforce a minimum zoom width, refresh incrementally.\n\nVotes: 1/1\n\nNodes: app-energy, store-sd-sports, drv-sd\n\n[[Gaps|Full gap register]]\nSource IDs (before rename mapping): app-energy, store-sports-journal, store-sd","color":"5"},
{"id":"gap-G60-component-0","type":"text","x":768,"y":103852,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Energy**\nDaily steps-based kcal, food and water…\n\nruns: UI task, only while it is the top screen (or in a transition). History refresh every 10 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Energy|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"gap-G60-component-1","type":"text","x":1224,"y":103852,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**SD sports journal (.spt)**\n/sdcard/watch/sports/YYYYMMDD-events.spt and…\n\nruns: SD. Drained every 1 s by sports_sd.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
